  "checks": [
    "One new generic module derives joint continuity from the existing real line MVT and a bound for the next jet on an open convex neighborhood selected after n,s,x. No common all-arity neighborhood is required.",
    "Positive jets are lifted with the existing genuine continuous multilinear circle realization; zero arity is the original f. The same scalar family supplies exact decoder equality and genuine projective line derivatives.",
    "The original endpointFlowCircle function and its decode/zero declarations remain byte-identical. Only its smooth-tower proof uses the new local-continuity interface. The theorem complete public header is unchanged.",
    "The state fixed-slot envelope explicitly returns parameterLoss before output s and directions. Its line envelope then uses the same energy at max base (s+loss+parameterLoss).",
    "The scalar line envelope keeps two genuinely fixed physical height localizations, with the parameter-order loss added only to their actual energy/grade order. Affine identities, integrability and square-sum envelope algebra are unchanged.",
    "Both zero-order circle-member proofs retain the same actual state/scalar curves, finite-order scalar derivatives and true weighted energy theorems. They select the first-derivative parameter loss before output s.",
    "All generic helper blocks in the four support files are byte-identical to their exact c5 predecessors. All qualitative public headers are preserved; the one exposed fixed-slot energy estimate honestly changes to n then parameterLoss then s.",
    "All selected imports, graph acyclicity and exact Git tree blob identities were checked statically. No old uniform-loss SectorFlowTower or EndpointParameterTower enters the closure."
  ],
